From 9d16f449eb277b94968e8466c42d1c7aa05716a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:38:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(microsoft): Graph mail, and the v1 authorization
 endpoint

Mail folders (well-known names included), messages kept as MIME (created
from MIME, served by $value), per-folder delta queries with paging and
removals, PATCH (read, flag, importance, categories), move, delete, and
sendMail (MIME or JSON) delivering to seeded users. Ids are immutable.

GET /:tenant/oauth2/authorize serves v1 (Azure AD) clients, mapping
their resource to its default scope, as the v1 token endpoint already
does.
