 ## Microsoft Graph
 
 The `/v1.0/me` endpoint returns an OData-style response with `displayName`, `mail`, `userPrincipalName`, and `id`.
+
+## Microsoft Graph Mail
+
+Each user's mailbox starts with the well-known folders (Inbox, Drafts, Sent Items, Deleted Items, Junk Email, Archive, Outbox). Messages are stored as MIME, created from MIME with `POST /v1.0/me/mailFolders/{folder}/messages` (the base64 source as a `text/plain` body), and served back by `$value`. Message ids never change, as with `Prefer: IdType="ImmutableId"`; `move` keeps them.
+
+`/messages/delta` on a folder lists its messages, then, from its `@odata.deltaLink`, those changed (read, flagged, importance, categories, moved in) or removed (moved out or deleted, as `@removed`) since. Pages hold 10 messages unless `Prefer: odata.maxpagesize=N` asks otherwise. An unknown delta token answers 410 `SyncStateNotFound`, as an expired one does.
+
+`sendMail` takes MIME (base64, `text/plain`) or a JSON `message`; it keeps a read copy in Sent Items (unless `saveToSentItems` is false) and delivers to each recipient that is a seeded user, without the `Bcc` header.
